# Lines the country test (country.bat) must write to COM1 with no
# COUNTRY= (scripts/smoke-test): MS-DOS 4.00's built-in United States
# settings. COUNTRY.SYS's data is Microsoft's (DEV/COUNTRY/MKCNTRY.ASM).

^GRDOS-TEST-BEGIN$
^== COUNTRY$
^COUNTRY 001 DATE 0 TIME 0 CURRENCY "\$" FORMAT 0 DIGITS 2$
^SEPARATORS THOUSANDS "," DECIMAL "\." DATE "-" TIME ":" LIST ","$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 437 SYSTEM 437$
^UPCASE 84 8E$
^Current date is \w{3} \d\d-\d\d-\d{4}$
^Enter new date \(mm-dd-yy\): $
^Current time is +\d+:\d\d:\d\d\.\d\d[ap]$
^NLSINFO  COM +544 \d\d-\d\d-\d\d +\d+:\d\d[ap]$

# NLSFUNC reads COUNTRY.SYS for CHCP, which changes the code page to 850:
# its uppercase table, the United Kingdom's, drops the diaeresis
^== NLSFUNC$
^Active code page: 437$
^Active code page: 850$
^COUNTRY 001 DATE 0 TIME 0 CURRENCY "\$" FORMAT 0 DIGITS 2$
^CODEPAGE ACTIVE 850 SYSTEM 437$
^UPCASE 84 41$
^GRDOS-TEST-END$
